    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this dispute goes to a human reviewer and the fare is held — neither refunded nor finally kept — until that review. The AI cannot close it (POL-GEN-26 and POL-RD-25).\n\nWhat the record shows. The recommended distance was 9.6 km and the recorded distance 10.9 km, a deviation of 1.30 km (13.5%) — over POL-RD-22's 1.0 km tolerance (EV-TRIP-05014; EV-FARE-05014's money block carries the same 1.30 km). The LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-05014-01 is an ACCIDENT on the KPE towards TPE, after the MacPherson Road exit, valid 21:06–22:16 — an admissible incident type, overlapping the trip window (21:16–21:38), on the recommended route's own road and at the very point the trace shows the vehicle leaving it (21:22:26). I therefore find it intersects the recommended route and that the reroute was traffic-justified under POL-RD-23; the rider's claim that justification is not established, and that row (d) therefore refunds the excess, is rejected. The driver's chat MSG-05014-003 (sent 21:19:56, read 21:20:23) preceded the deviation, so POL-RD-21's notice limb is met on the chat log.\n\nWhy there is no refund and no NO_ACTION. POL-RD-24(a) needs the rider to have agreed; row (b) needs her not to have been informed; row (d) needs the reroute not to have been traffic-justified. She was informed and the reroute was justified, so (b) and (d) are out. That leaves (a), which turns on her agreement — and the only acknowledgment is MSG-05014-004 ('aiyo can meh... ok lor whatever u say but dun charge me more ah'), in EV-CHAT-05014, which is impaired (issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY, weight 0.85) precisely because it mixes assent with a condition on the fare. The chat log does not confirm the acknowledgment POL-RD-21 requires, so agreement is not established and the case fits no row of POL-RD-24; POL-GEN-26 sends it to a human, and the driver's alternative escalation claim is accepted on that footing (his row-(a) NO_ACTION claim is rejected).\n\nIndependently, the confidence bar blocks a driver-favouring ruling. The rider's profile carries fraud_flags = 1 — a field POL-GEN-22 names — so an AI ruling here needs 0.95 confidence. POL-GEN-02(2) caps my confidence on the agreement fact at the 0.85 weight of the only artifact carrying it, which is below 0.95, and POL-RD-25 then escalates. (The driver's discarded version of this point failed only for not disclosing the 0.85 / LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY impairment; the rider's disclosed version is accepted.)\n\nOn the sums. The rider asks $4.20, but the only refund POL-RD-24 can ever award on these facts is the excess distance fare, 1.30 km × 0.72 SGD/km = 0.94 SGD (EV-FARE-05014), and on these findings the AI awards nothing at all. The contested $4.20 is held pending the human review. No clause of the loaded policy produces a referral, so none is entered."
