    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the fare is held and the case goes to a human reviewer. Here is why, and the one question the reviewer must answer.\n\nWhat is not in dispute. The trip ran 10.9 km against a recommended 9.6 km (POL-RD-22) — a deviation of 1.30 km, above the 1.0 km tolerance, so no 'within tolerance' outcome is available. The rider's point 1 is correct, and the sparse 9.226 km GPS trace is not used to re-measure the distance. The driver left the route at the KPE / MacPherson Road exit at 21:22:26 and rejoined at Hougang Avenue 3 / Upper Paya Lebar Road at 21:34:06; the driver-device trace EV-GPS-05014 shows those fixes. The metered fare charged was SGD 16.97.\n\nTraffic justification (POL-RD-23) — found. The LTA record EV-ADVIS-05014-01 (weight 1.0) is an ACCIDENT on the KPE towards TPE after the MacPherson Road exit, in force 21:06–22:16 on 3 September, which covers the trip window (21:16–21:38). The recommended route runs on the KPE and the driver left it at that very exit, so the advisory intersects the recommended route and overlaps the trip window. The reroute was traffic-justified. This rejects the rider's point 4: refund row (d) of POL-RD-24 needs the reroute to be unjustified, and it was justified.\n\nNotice (POL-RD-21) — given. The driver's MSG-05014-003 was sent 21:19:56, read 21:20:23 and states a brief reason, all before the 21:22:26 deviation; in-app chat is enough and no call recording is needed. The rider was informed, which removes refund row (b).\n\nAgreement (POL-RD-21) — not established, and this is the open question. The rider's reply MSG-05014-004 ('aiyo can meh... ok lor whatever u say but dun charge me more ah') mixes assent with a fare condition, and EV-CHAT-05014 is impaired for exactly that reason (issue code LANGUAGE_AMBIGUITY, weight_multiplier 0.85). POL-RD-21 makes a deviation 'agreed' only where the chat log confirms the rider's acknowledgment; this log does not. Row (a) is therefore not made out, and the case fits none of POL-RD-24's rows — the situation POL-GEN-26 sends to human review. The driver's point 3 is not accepted.\n\nConfidence — would have blocked a no-refund ruling in any event. A row (a) outcome turns on the acknowledgment, carried only by EV-CHAT-05014 at 0.85, so confidence on that fact is capped at 0.85 (POL-GEN-02(2)). The rider's profile carries a fraud flag (rider_profile.fraud_flags of 1), which raises the required confidence to 0.95 (POL-GEN-22), and POL-RD-25 makes the AI ruling stand only if POL-GEN-22 allows it. So no NO_ACTION can be entered and the driver's point 4 is not accepted.\n\nMoney. Nothing issues. The SGD 4.20 in dispute is held — neither collected from the rider nor refunded to her — and the SGD 16.97 fare stands for now. For reference, the most any refund row could yield is the excess distance fare: 1.30 km × 0.72 SGD/km = 0.94 SGD (POL-RD-24); the rider's claimed 4.20 SGD is not a figure this policy can produce.\n\nThe question for the reviewer: reading MSG-05014-004 together with the trip record, did the rider agree to the MacPherson Road reroute (which would leave the fare standing under row (a)), or object to the extra charge (which fits no row)? Until that is answered, no amount moves. No clause produces a referral on these facts."
